host_software/data/03_synthetic_yolo/
host_software/data/*_unified_pose/
host_software/data/yolo_raw_dataset/
host_software/data_collection/data/
host_software/data/*
# DVC pointer files for the reproducible-artifact tiers must stay trackable despite the
# blanket ignore above -- a trailing-slash "host_software/data/" exclusion (the previous
# form of this rule) makes git refuse to re-include ANYTHING inside it, .dvc files
# included, per git's own documented "can't re-include a file if a parent directory is
# excluded" rule. Using "host_software/data/*" (glob, not a directory exclusion) instead
# is what makes the negations below actually work. See docs/DATA_STORAGE.md.
!host_software/data/03_gold.dvc
!host_software/data/03_synthetic_yolo.dvc
!host_software/data/yolo_raw_dataset.dvc

host_software/ml_audio/data/

*.csv
evaluation_results/

generated/
logs/

